   "stem": {
      "text": "The density of plankton in a vertical column of lake water is modeled by \\( \\rho(h) = 10 \\sin{\\left(\\frac{h^{2}}{3} \\right)} + 60 \\) cells per cubic meter, where h is the depth below the surface in meters. Consider the column, which has horizontal cross-sections of constant area 12.25 square meters. Using a calculator, find the number of plankton cells in the column between the depths \\( h = 1 \\) and \\( h = 7 \\) meters. Show the setup, and give the value correct to three decimal places.",
      "setup_required": true,
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
